\\$308.02 million (for strategic investments) remaining unutilized, expected to be deployed by September 30, 2026.\n  * Hong Kong Corporate News\n\n# Knowledge Atlas Technology Completes HK$31.4 Billion H Share Placing to Fund AI R&D, Business Expansion, and Capital Optimization 2356\n\nPosted on July 14, 2026 at 7:51 pm (GMT+8)\n\nImage\n\nKnowledge Atlas Technology Joint Stock Company Limited: Completion of Placing of New H Shares\n\n# Knowledge Atlas Technology Joint Stock Company Limited: Completion of Placing of New H Shares Under General Mandate\n\n## Key Highlights and Investor-Relevant Details\n\n  * Successful Placing of New H Shares:\nKnowledge Atlas Technology Joint Stock Company Limited (“the Company”) has successfully completed the placing of 19,780,000 new H shares at HK\\$1,588.00 per share. This transaction was completed on July 13, 2026, following satisfaction of all conditions precedent stipulated in the placing agreement.\n  * Significant Capital Raise:\nThe aggregate gross proceeds from the placing amount to approximately HK\\$31,410.64 million, with net proceeds (after commissions and expenses) of approximately HK\\$31,374.95 million.   * Recent Equity Financing Activity:\nIn the past 12 months, the Company issued 43,043,400 new H shares as part of a global offering at HK\\$116.20 per share, raising net proceeds of HK\\$4,896.2 million. Most funds have been utilized, with only HK\\$308.02 million (for strategic investments) remaining unutilized, expected to be deployed by September 30, 2026.\n  * Price Sensitive Information:\n\n    * The placing price of HK\\$1,588.00 per H share is significantly higher than the previous global offering price (HK\\$116.20), indicating substantial investor confidence and potentially affecting share valuations.\n    * The substantial capital raise and allocation toward AI R&D, strategic investments, and working capital could materially impact the Company’s growth trajectory and market position.\n    * Changes in shareholding structure and the entry of new, independent institutional investors may affect liquidity and trading dynamics.\n    * The Company expects to fully utilize the net proceeds by the end of 2027, with unused funds to be held in interest-bearing accounts, ensuring prudent financial management.\n    * 30%用於優化資本結構及營運資金： 用於日常營運、銷售市場推廣、專業費用、償還短期負債及維持流動性。\n  * 研發策略：\n公司致力於人工智能基礎模型領域的技術領先，重點包括：\n\n    * 長周期任務能力（模型可處理數週至數月的任務）\n    * 全自動代理系統（數千數碼員工代理）\n    * AI訓練AI（自我進化、合成數據、自我對抗訓練）\n    * 安全及超級對齊機制（機理可解釋性、ESG管理）\n    * 安全領域人才擴展\n    * 提升計算資源調度與管理\n  * 策略投資及生態擴展：\n目標收購AI相關業務，如成熟平台、穩定運營、強管理團隊及增長潛力，並加強技術及渠道合作，擴大市場。\n  * 近期股權融資：\n過去12個月曾以每股HK\\$116.20發行43,043,400股H股，籌得淨款HK\\$4,896.2百萬元，多數已用，剩餘HK\\$308.02百萬元（策略投資）預計於2026年9月前動用。\n  * 價格敏感資訊：\n\n    * 配售價遠高於上次全球發售價，顯示市場信心，或對股價有正面影響。\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nZhipu Completes Approximately $5 Billion Financing for Next-Generation GLM Development | insigtX (https://www.insigtx.com/en/news/zhipu-completes-approximately-5-billion-financing-for-next-169665/)\nciteturn772search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 days ago; Crawled: 2 days ago; On September 13, according to Jinshi Data, Zhipu (02513. ...     September 13, 2026 10:31 UTC ... HK) announced the completion of approximately $5 billion in financing, comprising a $2 billion share placement and $3 billion in convertible bonds.\n\nCrypto insigtX\n\n# Zhipu Completes Approximately $5 Billion Financing for Next-Generation GLM Development\n\nOn September 13, according to Jinshi Data, Zhipu (02513.HK) announced the completion of approximately $5 billion in financing, comprising a $2 billion share placement and $3 billion in…\n\nPublished\n    September 13, 2026 10:31 UTC\nMarket\n    Crypto\nSource\n    insigtX\n\nOn September 13, according to Jinshi Data, Zhipu (02513.HK) announced the completion of approximately $5 billion in financing, comprising a $2 billion share placement and $3 billion in convertible bonds. The funds will be directed toward next-generation GLM model R&D, self-training systems, and computing infrastructure.\n\nThe share placement price is HK$714, representing a discount of approximately 9.96% to the previous closing price, accounting for about 4.50% of the enlarged share capital. The convertible bonds carry a zero-coupon structure with an issue price at 100.5% of principal, and an initial conversion price of HK$892.50, representing a 25% premium to the placement price and approximately 12.55% premium to the previous closing price. This combination of zero-coupon and premium is seen as signaling long-term equity expectations. Upon fund deployment, Zhipu's capital base for enhancing its computing infrastructure is strengthened, adding leverage for competing in global frontier model competition.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHong Kong — 9 September 2026 | algo2alpha — The Learning Investor (https://www.algo2alpha.com/p/hk/2026-09-09/)\nciteturn772search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6 days ago; Crawled: 2 days ago; 2513  | KNOWLEDGE ATLAS  | 913.50  | SELL 85.46%  | 913.50  | 847.45  | 965.06 (+5.6%)  | 1034.34 (+13.2%)  | 1103.38 (+20.8%)  | Z.AI broke decisively below the risk line we had set for it and has not recovered, while carrying the strongest sell reading in the book for a second straight session. ... Event risk: 09-11 Oracle Q1 FY2027 read-through and 09-14 US CPI both touch this name — de-risking before them, not into them.\n2513  | KNOWLEDGE ATLAS  | 913.50  | SELL 85.46%  | 913.50  | 847.45  | 965.06 (+5.6%)  | 1034.34 (+13.2%)  | 1103.38 (+20.8%)  | Z.AI broke decisively below the risk line we had set for it and has not recovered, while carrying the strongest sell reading in the book for a second straight session. It is our largest liquid holding at roughly 17% of the portfolio and sits 44% below cost, so we are cutting 80% of it and keeping a small stub. We are honest that the model's own 12-week pr